    {
      "skill_id": "fr-a1-005",
      "title": "Frequent irregular verbs: aller, faire, prendre",
      "explanation": "A few of the most frequent French verbs do not follow the regular -er pattern, so learn their present forms as units. Aller (to go): je vais, tu vas, il/elle/on va, nous allons, vous allez, ils/elles vont. Faire (to do, to make): je fais, tu fais, il/elle/on fait, nous faisons, vous faites, ils/elles font. Prendre (to take, also to have food or drink or to use transport): je prends, tu prends, il/elle/on prend, nous prenons, vous prenez, ils/elles prennent. Aller is the verb for going somewhere and is followed by à and the place: Je vais à Lyon.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "fr": "Je vais à la maison.",
          "en": "I am going home."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Nous faisons du sport.",
          "en": "We do sport."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Elle prend le bus.",
          "en": "She takes the bus."
        }
      ],
