    {
      "skill_id": "fr-a1-008",
      "title": "Question words: qui, où, quand, comment, pourquoi, combien",
      "explanation": "Common question words are qui (who), où (where), quand (when), comment (how), pourquoi (why) and combien (how many, how much). A reliable pattern is the question word followed by est-ce que and a normal statement: Où est-ce que tu habites ? Before a vowel, est-ce que becomes est-ce qu': Pourquoi est-ce qu'elle travaille ? In informal speech the question word can also come first with normal word order (Où tu habites ?) or last (Tu habites où ?). With être, the question word often comes straight before the verb: Où est Marie ? Qui est là ?",
      "examples": [
        {
          "fr": "Où est-ce que tu habites ?",
          "en": "Where do you live?"
        },
        {
          "fr": "Pourquoi est-ce que vous mangez ici ?",
          "en": "Why are you eating here?"
        },
        {
          "fr": "Qui est-ce ?",
          "en": "Who is it?"
        }
      ],
      "references": ["FEI-INV"],
